# Sedges: low fountains of fine, arching leaves drooping at their tips, yellow-olive, along a river's banks and a lake's
# shore - most in slow water, a few beside faster water too. No stalk (Head Tuft: 8 leaves of two slots each). Format:
# Code/Procedural/CONTEXT.md, "Ground clutter".
ClutterType Sedge
	Kind Flower
	Seed 223
	Scale 0.7 1.2
	Range 90
	Color 0.52 0.55 0.25
	Color2 0.22 0.17 0.10
	Head Tuft
	Petals 10
	Open 40
	PetalWidth 0.7
	Stem 1
	HeadSize 0.05
	Placement
		Density 62
		Temperature 2 35
		River 0 1 3
		Flow 1 0.25
		# on the banks, hardly any under the water
		Water 1 0.00
		Cluster 5 0.6
		Slope 0.8
		Altitude -1000
